      <h2>Introduction: Why Did Omegle Shut Down?</h2>

      <p>Omegle, the random-chat website that connected strangers without requiring traditional profiles, shut down in November 2023 after more than 14 years online.</p>

      <p>The closure surprised many people because Omegle had become one of the best-known names in random online conversation. However, the shutdown was not simply the result of one technical problem or one new law. The decision came after years of challenges involving misuse of the service, moderation, operating costs, legal pressure, and the personal burden of running the platform.</p>

      <p>Omegle founder Leif K-Brooks explained his decision in a lengthy statement published when the service closed. His explanation is important because it provides first-hand context that is often missing from simplified summaries of the shutdown.</p>

      <p>This article examines what happened, when Omegle shut down, what the founder said about the decision, the major challenges surrounding the platform, and what its closure means for people looking for random chat and Omegle alternatives today.</p>

