      <h2>4. What Did Omegle's Founder Say?</h2>

      <p>The founder's own explanation is one of the most important sources for understanding the shutdown.</p>

      <p>Leif K-Brooks explained that operating Omegle had become extremely difficult because of the abuse of the service and the costs associated with trying to address that abuse. He also described the personal burden of running the platform and the difficulty of dealing with the consequences of misuse.</p>

      <p>This distinction matters. The shutdown was not presented simply as “Omegle was banned.” Instead, the founder described a broader decision to stop operating the service after years of challenges.</p>

      <h3>What This Means</h3>

      <p>It is therefore more accurate to describe Omegle's closure as a business and operational decision shaped by safety, misuse, legal pressure and the costs and responsibilities of continuing the service.</p>

      <p>Statements such as “Omegle was shut down because of one specific law” oversimplify the situation.</p>

      <h2>5. The Main Factors Behind Omegle's Closure</h2>

